<title>USA: Iowa-So Minn hogs estimate Wednesday 100,000 - USDA.</title>
<headline>Iowa-So Minn hogs estimate Wednesday 100,000 - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>DES MOINES 1997-02-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Wednesday's estimated interior Iowa/southern Minnesota hog marketings were 100,000 head, compared with 104,000 a week ago and 105,000 a year ago, USDA said. Estimates include generally about 60 percent Carcass Base Hogs.</p>
<p>Barrows and gilts were steady to $0.50 per cwt higher than midsession Tuesday. Trade moderate for good demand and light to moderate offerings.</p>
<p>				  Country		    Plant</p>
<p>US 1-3   46-49% Carcass Base Lean*</p>
<p>220-260 lbs	    49.50 -50.50	   50.50 -51.50</p>
<p>few			49.00  51.00	   50.00  52.00</p>
<p>US 1-3   46-49% Carcass Base Lean*</p>
<p>260-280 lbs	    47.50 -50.50	   48.00 -51.50</p>
<p>US 2-4   43-49% Carcass Base Lean</p>
<p>280-300 lbs	    44.00 -50.50	   44.50 -51.50</p>
<p>Sows:  mostly steady to 1.00 higher.</p>
<p>US 1-3 300-450 lbs.  40.00 -42.00	   41.50 -43.00</p>
<p>450-500 lbs.	   43.00 -45.00	   44.00 -46.00</p>
<p>500 lbs. up	    49.00 -51.50	   50.00 -52.50</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk 312-408-8720))</p>
